<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hassanal Bolkiah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1946</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hassanal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolkiah">Bolkiah</a> is the sultan of Brunei, who succeeded his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/omar-ali-saifuddien-iii">Omar Ali Saifuddien III</a> in 1967. He led the country to full independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> in 1984 and has since also served as prime minister and held other key ministries. One of the world's longest-reigning monarchs, he rules an absolute monarchy whose wealth rests on oil and gas.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hassanal-bolkiah.jpg" alt="Hassanal Bolkiah" width="320" height="426" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cancillería del Perú · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Visita_de_Estado_del_Sult%C3%A1n_de_Brun%C3%A9i_Darussalam,_Hassanal_Bolkiah_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
